.TH DISPLAY.CONF 5
.SH NAME
display.conf, .look, .mouse \- the desktop's settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/display.conf
.br
.B ~/.look
.br
.B ~/.mouse
.SH DESCRIPTION
The desktop,
.BR atlas (4),
keeps what its Settings window chooses in small files of
.IB key = value
lines.
.TP
.B /etc/display.conf
the machine's, the login screen's too:
.RS
.TP
.BI size= W x H
the screen size, where the screen can take any (QEMU's VGA and ramfb, the
Pi 4, the Intel display); by default 1920x1080
.TP
.BI brightness= N
the panel's backlight, in % (the Intel display)
.TP
.BR lid=sleep " or " lid=off
what closing a laptop's lid does: sleep, or the screen off
.RE
.TP
.B ~/.look
the user's own, applied at login:
.B look=
the look's number (Phosphor, Amber 1984, Glass, BeOS; Phosphor before a
login) and
.B zoom=
the size of everything in % (50 to 400, 100 by default)
.TP
.B ~/.mouse
the user's own, applied at login:
.B speed=
the pointer's speed in % (25 to 400, 100 by default),
.B swap=1
left-handed buttons,
.B reverse=1
the wheel reversed
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR atlas (4),
.BR con (4)
